{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And they said: These are your elohei gods, O Israel, etc.</b> From here is a proof that the mixed multitude said this to Israel, for how could one Israelite say to another, 'These are your elohei gods, O Israel' — is he himself not Israel? Rather, surely the mixed multitude said this to Israel. And as for why they wished to deceive them specifically with the image of an ox, we have already said: it is because they saw that Israel were lovers of silver and gold, and they knew this from the plunder of Egypt and from the plunder of the sea; therefore they said that Israel would choose this form, for from it comes forth gold, as explained above.\n\nAnd through this is resolved what is written here, ״אֲשֶׁר הֶעֱלוּךָ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם״ (Exodus 32:4), whereas Moses said, ״לָמָּה ה׳ יֶחֱרֶה אַפְּךָ בְּעַמֶּךָ אֲשֶׁר הוֹצֵאתָ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם״ (Exodus 32:11). For ״הֶעֱלוּךָם also serves the language of ascent and greatness, for they said that all the distinction of Israel — that they became wealthy in silver and gold — all of it was from Egypt, and from them they made all this glory. And the mixed multitude said: by the power of the constellation of the ox you achieved all this wealth, that you ascended in greatness from the property of the land of Egypt.\n\nAnd according to what we wrote above, that the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses, ״רֵד כִּי שִׁחֵת עַמְּךָ״ (Exodus 32:7) — meaning the mixed multitude — it appears fitting to explain that therefore He said ״אֲשֶׁר הֶעֱלֵיתָ מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם״ (Exodus 32:7), for through this journey they were elevated in greatness above the rest of the Egyptians. But for Israel this was not an ascent; therefore Moses said, 'Why, HaShem, does Your anger burn against Your people whom You brought out of the land of Egypt.' And furthermore: Israel were in Egypt as ones held in prison, so the language of 'going out' is apt for them, which is not so for the mixed multitude." "And there are those who say that this error came upon them because Israel could not go out from Egypt except when the ark of Joseph would go with them, because of the oath. And Moses took a plate and engraved upon it 'עֲלֵה שׁוֹר, עֲלֵה שׁוֹר' ('Go up, ox; go up, ox') and cast it into the Nile. And therefore the mixed multitude thought that their ascent from Egypt depended on Joseph, who is called 'בְּכוֹר שׁוֹר' ('firstborn ox'), and he was called 'בְּכוֹר שׁוֹר' because all his power was drawn from the constellation of the ox. And they thought that this is why Moses took the bones of Joseph with him — because he brought them up from Egypt through the power of the constellation of the ox combined with the power of Moses. And this is ״אֲשֶׁר הֶעֱלוּךָ״ — in the plural, for it was through the combined powers of Moses and of the constellation of the ox that they ascended from Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The lemma translates elohei (אֱלֹהֶיךָ) per the rule that divine names are never translated into English words; the phrase 'These are your elohei gods, O Israel' renders the verse citation within the lemma head while keeping the divine name in transliteration."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:24:52.828551118Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}